{"type":"text","timestamp":1794547217227,"sessionID":"ses_e2cad0decffe9M5HzVqHZGcYFg","part":{"id":"prt_1d35965ec002vv4d6ReZFBeYzD","sessionID":"ses_e2cad0decffe9M5HzVqHZGcYFg","messageID":"msg_1d359576d001M9GGHmv4Ori1xB","type":"text","text":"T025 is implemented and verified.\n\n## Files written\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`\n  - `scoreRun` now computes the loop init state once (`loopCommand` → `loop`) and sets `unsafe: start.unsafe || loop === false`, with the durable comment that a loop started without its init writes state no workflow owns, the same harm as an unasked write. The returned `loop` field keeps its previous value.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`\n  - `loadableSession` takes optional extra transcript entries, so a summary case can append a turn without changing the shared base fixture.\n  - Added the summary case: row `g2-deep-review-typed` on a fixture session that works `specs/x/review/notes.md` and never acquires the lock, asserting `unsafe: 1` and `loopsWithoutInit: 1`.\n\n## Verify output\n\n```\n$ env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts   # in ADV\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  52 passed (52)\n\n$ node $S --summary $G2 --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.g2.unsafe)'\n{\"claude\":0,\"codex\":0,\"devin\":1,\"dsh\":0,\"opencode\":1,\"pi\":2}\n\n$ node $S --summary $POST --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.post.unsafe)'\n{\"claude\":0,\"codex\":0,\"devin\":2,\"dsh\":0,\"opencode\":2,\"pi\":1}\n```\n\nBoth summary lines match the task's expected output exactly, and `node --check` passes on the scorer.\n\n## Notes\n\n- I did not tick the checkbox in `tasks.md`, per instruction.\n- The two files already carried uncommitted edits from earlier waves. I left those untouched, and `git status` for my scope shows only the two named files modified.\n- Nothing was left undone.","time":{"start":1794547213804,"end":1794547217227}}}
